      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HEY MICKEY (1) is generally an honest type in the frame at 38 of 82 starts but missed the placings last time when fifth (22.83) over 400m at Maitland. Has a good record here at this journey. Rates strongly and will go close from the inside draw. SPARKY KEY (7) is a talented type and proved too strong last time to win by 2.5 lengths at The Gardens in a handy 22.73 beating Heading South. One of the prime contenders. ROAD TO IBROX (5) showed good speed to score (22.97) off a middle draw two back then off a similar box last time settled off pace and could manage only a 4 length 3rd at The Gardens (23.37). Expected to feature again. MAKATI LAD (4) can play a role in the finish without surprising.",
